From: FE Fates port <engine@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] core: Fire Emblem Fates randomizer: names and voices in
 messages (the full swap's trap in Mess::Get)

Round 74 (docs/ROUND74_PLAN.md A4, docs/rando/FULL_BLOCK.md section 4,
docs/rando/FULL_SWAP_PLAN.md section 2, owner OK "Yes, start round 74"): new
module fates_rando_names. Mess::Get (0x003D1CEC; the label kept in r7 from
0x003D1CF4) returns through 0x003D1DA8 on all three paths (label not found
from 0x003D1D18, a plain message from 0x003D1D90, a built message from
0x003D1DA4) with the text in r0; the word there is add sp, sp, #80
(0xE28DD050, then pop {r4-r8, pc}; read from the owner's dump).

While a randomized run whose folder holds full.txt (rando.py make
--patch-out writes it beside patch.txt only for look = full; make_run_inner
keeps it with the run like nuzlocke.json) with something for this game's
text language (E) is active, the frame hook writes a reserved svc
(0xEFFEC002; 0xFEC001 is round 71's chest trap) over that word with
write32_privileged and has the recompiled code checked again, so the
interpreter runs Mess::Get. kernel::svc::dispatch hands the svc to on_svc:
at 0x003D1DA8 only (ARM, the cpu past the svc) it does the add itself and,
unless the label starts with MPID_ (person names and help texts: the table
cells already point them at the filler's own labels), passes the UTF-16
text at r0 through one pass: commands ($, a name from a counted table, its
arguments) are copied, except $Svp commands whose label starts with
VOICE_<key>_ for a silenced key, which are dropped; plain text gets every
whole-word old name replaced, all pairs at once, longest first, never
chained; full_off_chapters (empty this round) pass everything, the chapter
being the last chapter person file in the Person list (else GameUserData's).
A changed text is written into the core's own ring of buffers and r0 points
there; the message file and the game's shared buffer are never written.

The ring: guest addresses 0x50000000-0x500FFFFF, mapped by the core the
first time a full run arms the trap, pages from FCRAM's Base region (as the
HLE services' shared memory). Free: a 3DS process is never given an address
at or above 0x40000000 (every region the game or Zakuro maps lies below it),
and the core maps only when Memory::mapping_at finds nothing over the range
(else the trap stays off with a notice). Each changed text takes the next
4-aligned bytes, wrapping, so the 36 callers that keep two results at once
(round 73b) keep both. Once mapped it stays mapped, so a held pointer never
dangles.

Off means original: no full.txt (look = keep: every run the owner's page can
make, every run before round 74, Randomizer off), nothing for this language
and no voice key, a file that does not parse (notice "dialogue names kept
(full.txt: <reason>)"), another seed or another game: neither word
(0x003D1DA8, 0x003D1784) is ever written and no memory is mapped. The original word goes back when
the run ends; a save state holding the svc is put right the same way.

New tests the_file_is_read_whole_or_refused,
no_file_or_another_language_only_means_off,
names_are_whole_words_in_one_pass_and_never_chain,
a_silenced_speaker_goes_quiet_and_another_is_kept,
commands_are_never_touched_and_a_command_next_to_a_name_is_a_word_break,
the_ring_wraps_and_keeps_the_last_two_results,
the_trap_changes_a_line_and_leaves_names_and_untouched_texts,
an_off_chapter_passes_everything,
the_word_follows_the_pass_and_leaves_a_stranger_alone,
both_places_are_trapped_and_their_labels_are_found,
a_built_message_is_returned_as_the_game_built_it,
a_repeated_text_shares_one_copy_while_it_is_young (made-up names, lines
and labels only).

Round 74 repair (the one repair build B2, after the robot's P2 proof
failed on this patch): story scenes and support talks are fetched through
Mess::GetNoReplace (0x003D16CC, push {r4-r6, lr}; callers
ProcTalkManager::Initialize and TalkExpander::ExpandMessage(const char*)),
which returns through its own 0x003D1784 (add sp, sp, #80, the same word,
then pop {r4-r6, pc}) and never passed the trap: names stayed A's and A's
$Svp commands stayed. The svc is now written at both places (TRAP_SITES;
on_svc tells them apart by the address; the recompiled code is checked
again when either word changes). GetNoReplace keeps no label register (r5
is reloaded at 0x003D1720), so the label is read from the "<label>_COM"
both functions print into their stack buffer at sp (format 0x00644CF8).
Second, a built Mess::Get text (the message at r4 starts with $a: the game
filled in arguments, the person names already the filler's through the
table cells) is now returned as built; passing it again chained B -> C
("Kaze and Rinkah attained support level B." where keep said "Kaze and
Hana"). Third, a changed text already in the younger half of the ring
with the same bytes is handed out again instead of written again (the
talk manager keeps a scene's text for the whole scene, and a menu may
fetch the same text every frame).
